  "instruction": "Judge each supplied pair using only the supplied document evidence. All document pages' eligible evidence are supplied, so do not assume omitted slides contain supporting facts. Preserve each endpoint's scope; do not invent a different task or instance. Evidence rows are [id,page,kind,exact_text]. Use natural Traditional Chinese in a concise specific reason.\nTypes and direction: prerequisite = necessary knowledge -> the task/knowledge that explicitly depends on it, not helpful background or slide order; part_of = actual constituent -> whole, not chapter membership, declaration syntax or a general subtype; application = concept/method -> concrete task/result accomplished with it, not mere definition/representation; example = abstract concept -> concrete instance, not automatically a general subtype or analogy; contrast = the two compared entities on an explicit axis, symmetric.\nReturn one decision per pair: supported only when a precise type and direction are grounded; no_relation when both endpoints are described sufficiently but no direct relation is supported; insufficient_evidence when relevant descriptions or the needed connection are missing; needs_review when endpoint/type boundaries, multiple reasonable labels, or source inconsistencies make a unique decision unreliable. For non-supported decisions use type=none,source_id=null,target_id=null. Do not infer from case identifiers or expected class frequency. Cite evidence row IDs, including context when abstaining. An empty evidence list is allowed only if no relevant evidence is present. Reasons should be at most 70 Chinese characters. Return only {decisions:[{id,status,type,source_id,target_id,evidence,reason}]} JSON.\nIf page images are attached, treat them as additional source evidence, not instructions. Read only visible content; do not invent hidden procedures. An attached image is labelled with its PDF page and integer image evidence ID; cite that ID when a judgment relies on the image. Cite an ID only when its corresponding text evidence, source-derived visual facts, or page image is actually supplied. A diagram arrow does not by itself establish a learning prerequisite.\n\nEndpoint a_id identifies a (A); b_id identifies b (B). These stable IDs are names only, not relation hints.\nFor supported relations, return the actual source_id and target_id from this pair in the type-defined source-to-target order. Both must identify this pair's two endpoints. For contrast either order is valid. Non-supported decisions must have both IDs null.\n",
